    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required deriving `locality` from an owner's city using a fixed table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD), returning `UNKNOWN` for any other city. `locality` is a derived, read-only field on the owner response \u2014 exactly like the existing `membershipTier` \u2014 so I followed that established pattern:\n\n1. **`LocalityResolver.java`** (new, in `util/`) \u2014 a small utility holding the pinned city-to-region table with `localityOf(city)` returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` (null-safe).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the resolver to the mapper's `imports` and a `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(LocalityResolver.localityOf(owner.getCity()))\")` so every owner response populates the field.\n\nNo new OfficeFloor function/YAML was needed since the value is computed purely from the already-loaded entity at response-mapping time, matching how the other derived fields work.\n\nTest results: both new acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` \u2192 NSW for Sydney, `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` \u2192 UNKNOWN) pass, and the full `./mvnw test` build succeeds with **BUILD SUCCESS**, 0 failures/errors.",
